WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.500
(Tommy narrating) I gotta go to the bank, and grab a little bit of money.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.500
♪ [bumper music]

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.000
(Tommy live) How am I supposed to do this now - like this?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.500
So, what we're gonna do is go to the ATM.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.500
(Tommy live) It doesn't give me much time. Why didn't that work?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.250
Oh.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.500
I got a pair of headphones with me, so I can plug in.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.250
Plug 'em in, standard headset jack.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.500
It's on the ATM for spoken instructions.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.000
It takes a little bit longer for me than sighted people.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.000
(Tommy live) It tells me to plug them in, but it doesn't tell me where to plug them in.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.500
Take cash below - that doesn't work.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.500
Jack. Ring-a-ding-ding.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.000
(Tommy narrating) Normally, when there's - like there's little circle around the headphone jack or something.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.500
It's pretty recognizable.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
(Tommy live) Jack below.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.000
There. No?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.500
And you know, when the braille says "right below", I'm thinking right below.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.000
But it was a couple of things below.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Way below, like down here below? No.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.000
Maybe down there below? Why would they put that up there for that?

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.000
What the - why is it so complicated for me?

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.000
Why can't I find the stupid hole?

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.250
Oy vey.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.000
(Tommy narrating) The simplest thing in the world, but I couldn't find it because it was sort of camouflaged.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.500
 I promise you, it was camouflaged.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.000
(Tommy live) There's a hole there with nothing, there's nothing in between the holes.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.000
Tommy narrating) I just started to push the headphone in, just randomly, into places - just push, push push.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.000
(Tommy live) ...as is that. Nothing plugs in anywhere.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.000
Unless it plugs in there.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.000
Oh, it scared me.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.000
Wow, it doesn't feel like a hole at all, does it?

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.000
(ATM) This ATM provides spoken instructions for your convenience.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.750
For a tutorial, press enter on the keypad.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Hopefully, nobody's gonna be impatient, and be banging on the door....

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.000
"Come on, already, hurry up!"

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.000
(ATM) The keypad is located to the lower left of the headphone jack,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
approximately 7 inches at 7 o'clock.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.500
One time I was at an ATM, and this woman just being as loud as can be,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.750
"ohhh".

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.000
(ATM) The keypad consists of 16 keys.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.000
There are 4 rows of keys with 4 keys on each row.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.000
The left 3 columns of keys are identical to a telephone keypad,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.000
with the number 1 in the upper left.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.000
I was like, you know what lady, I can't see, alright? Calm down.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
I'll be out of here in a min - I'm trying to catch a train.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.000
(ATM) Insert your card with the raised print facing up.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
into the left side of the slot.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Please enter your pin using the keypad.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.750
[keypad beeping]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.000
(ATM) Select enter to continue.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.000
[more beeping] 

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.000
(ATM) Enter

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
For withdrawal, press enter.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.750
[beep]

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.500
Enter

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.500
Normally when you enter numbers, like if you do it on a phone, they want it in dollars and cents.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Like, say you want 400 dollars, you go "four double zero double zero"

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
(ATM) Four zero zero zero zero

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Enter. You have exceeded the limit that this ATM can dispense.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.000
I took off the 2 zeros...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
(ATM) Four zero zero 

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.000
(Tommy) Let's try this.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.000
[cash dispenser wheels spinning]

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
There we go.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.750
So now I have money. So now we can go have a couple of refreshments.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.066
(ATM) Thank you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.000
(Tommy) Thank you.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.000
[beep]

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.000
♪ [bumper music]

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.000
If you wanna do this, please do this. Now this action is because of this.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.500
This key with the circle does this. This one with the line, the universal sign of a line

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:50.500
Then they're talking about a universal sign of a plus sign? I've never seen that before in my life.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.000
I don't know from a -- I know X, circle, straight line.

